   "source": "# Benchmark Model 3 — Ada-DF (Modern FER Method)\n**EmpathBot · CS731 Group 14 | Preeti · TJ · Kanishka**\n\n---\n\n### What this notebook does\nDownloads **Ada-DF** pre-trained weights (or trains from scratch if no public weights exist)  \nand evaluates on **RAF-DB** and **AffectNet** — the two datasets most relevant to EmpathBot.\n\nAda-DF is a modern FER method that uses adaptive feature fusion to handle the distribution  \nshift problem between lab-collected datasets and real-world faces. Including it as a benchmark  \nshows the reviewers we are aware of 2023–24 developments beyond just POSTER++.\n\n### Two evaluation datasets\n| Dataset | Classes | Test set size | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| RAF-DB | 7 standard | 3,068 | Same dataset POSTER++ uses → direct comparison |\n| AffectNet | 8 standard | ~3,500 (val) | Closest to EmpathBot's training data → shows real-world relevance |\n\n### Inputs\n| File / folder | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `data/RAF-DB/basic/Image/aligned/` | RAF-DB pre-aligned faces |\n| `data/RAF-DB/basic/EmoLabel/list_patition_label.txt` | RAF-DB labels |\n| `data/processed/affectnet/` | AffectNet images (from pipeline notebook 1) |\n| `data/master_split.csv` | EmpathBot master split (for AffectNet test split) |\n| `Ada-DF/` | Cloned Ada-DF repo (auto-created) |\n| `models/ada_df_rafdb.pth` | Pre-trained checkpoint |\n\n### Outputs\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `results/ada_df_rafdb_results.json` | RAF-DB accuracy, F1, per-class |\n| `results/ada_df_affectnet_results.json` | AffectNet accuracy, F1, per-class |\n| `results/ada_df_confusion_matrices.png` | Side-by-side confusion matrices |\n| `results/ada_df_comparison_table.png` | All three benchmarks side by side |"
