   "source": "---\n## Cell 3 — What is Ada-DF?\n\n**Ada-DF** (Adaptive Distribution-aware Feature learning) is a modern FER approach that  \naddresses one of POSTER++'s core limitations: distribution mismatch between training  \ndatasets and real-world deployment conditions.\n\n**The problem Ada-DF solves:**  \nDatasets like RAF-DB and AffectNet have systematically different face distributions —  \ndifferent camera angles, lighting, age ranges, and cultural expression norms. Models  \ntrained on one dataset often perform 5–15% worse on another. Ada-DF uses adaptive  \nweighting to learn which features are more transferable across datasets.\n\n**Architecture overview:**\n- A **ViT or ResNet** backbone for initial feature extraction\n- An **adaptive feature selector** that weights feature channels based on distribution  \n  statistics (mean, variance) computed per batch\n- A **dual-branch fusion** module: one branch captures global expression features,  \n  the other captures local facial region features (AU-aware)\n- **Distribution-aware loss**: cross-entropy + feature alignment term\n\n**Why include Ada-DF as a benchmark:**  \nIt represents methods that go beyond single-dataset FER and learn more generalisable  \nfacial features — exactly the challenge EmpathBot faces when deploying on live webcam.\n\n> **Note:** If Ada-DF refers to a specific paper in your literature review, update  \n> `ADADF_REPO_URL` in Cell 4 to match that paper's official GitHub. The evaluation  \n> framework (Cells 7–12) works for any FER model."
